+## engine-93 (by merge order): the clock is his intent, his eyes are its execution (2026-11-24)
+
+On: `QB_STEP_CLOCK` (QB lane; Integration's card). READ_WINDOW and the quick clock ride on it.
+
+Off, the drop ended on its 0.4 s overtime more often than on arrival (phase set p50 1.45 s on a quick drop called for
+0.75 s; 2.30 s on a five called for 1.4), and every later read counted from that late set. A read's time was a dwell set
+by decision-making, so the best reader moved on fastest: he left 61% of reads before his eyes had been on the man for
+0.2 s.
+
+On:
+- **The plant.** He plants at his set point or on the drop's count from the snap, whichever comes first, and each read's
+  step lands n strides after it.
+- **A look resolves.** From when his clear cone holds the man, resolved = 1 − e^(−dwell/τ).
+  - τ comes from playRecognition, decisionMaking and experience.
+  - It is slower when pressure narrows him, and when his post-snap belief disagrees with his pre-snap one.
+  - An unresolved look adds 0.5 yd × (1 − resolved) to the window's spreads for the receiver and the men on him.
+- **He moves on when sure.** At a read's step he moves on only when resolved ≥ his need (composure, discipline), and felt
+  pressure lowers the need.
+
+Rating panel (staged, 256 plays per row), from the clock's own log of the reads he left:
+
+| passer | resolved when he left | need | reads held past their step | held p50 / p90 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| dart (fair processing, low composure and discipline) | 0.48 | 0.45 | 34% | 0.05 / 0.15 s |
+| high | 0.78 | 0.74 | 57% | 0.15 / 0.35 s |
+| stare (slow processing, high composure and discipline) | 0.75 | 0.74 | 76% | 0.30 / 0.45 s |
+
+League, 8 games, against engine-92 (not paired; the card is the test):
+
+| | engine-92 | with QB_STEP_CLOCK |
+|---|---|---|
+| completion | 68.5% | 67.6% |
+| INT | 11 | 8 |
+| sacks | 36 | 38 |
+| time to throw p50 | 2.75 s | 2.65 s |
+| gun 2–3.5 yd set | 2.00 s at 3.03 yd | 1.90 s at 2.69 yd (NFL 2.00 s, 2.78 yd) |
+| under-centre set depth | 6.27 yd | 4.60 yd (NFL 3.70) |
+
+A first form held play-action sets to the fake's full count (play-action sacks 12 → 21). It was fixed before these
+runs.
